Here's the answer, thanks to Kamil Barton, for anyone else who may be in a similar bind in the future:

The unmarked thread I had previously linked <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/unmarked/d0p_c9W_kRo> to wasn't entirely correct. The formula syntax isn't appropriate for my needs, as it keeps one component of the occupancy model fixed (in this case, the detection component) and does not dredge the other component. To keep the detection component fixed and dredge the occupancy component, the subset expression should instead be a character vector:
pdredge(global_occ, rank=AIC, m.max=5, cluster=clust, fixed=c("p(Freq)", "p(I(Freq^2))", "p(n)", "p(mean_tree_d9)", "p(mean_tree_kurt)"))

