No, occupancy is assumed to be constant across the visits. So having a covariate that changes each visit for occupancy won't do anything. Detection can vary due to covariates that are constant among visits at a site or otherwise considered a site attribute, which is why I'm guessing you can make the site_cov part of the detection model.

